subtract|take-away-number|VERB|remove an amount from a total|To take a number or amount away from another in a calculation.|trừ đi|Subtract the delivery charge from the total to find the price of the goods.|Trừ phí giao hàng khỏi tổng số tiền để tính giá hàng hóa.|Transitive; subtract A from B gives B minus A, so the order matters.|-
warehouse|storage-building|NOUN|building for storing goods|A large building where goods are kept before they are sold or sent elsewhere.|nhà kho|The bicycles stayed in the warehouse until the shop had space for them.|Những chiếc xe đạp được giữ trong nhà kho cho đến khi cửa hàng có chỗ.|Countable; in a warehouse identifies the storage location.|0
daisy|flower|NOUN|small flower with a central disk|A small flowering plant whose flower usually has a yellow centre surrounded by white petals.|hoa cúc nhỏ; cây cúc dại|A daisy grew through a gap beside the garden path.|Một cây cúc dại mọc lên qua khe hở cạnh lối đi trong vườn.|Countable; the plural is daisies. The word may name the plant or its flower.|-
flag|cloth-symbol|NOUN|cloth symbol of a group|A piece of cloth with a distinctive design used to represent a country, organization, or other group.|lá cờ|The club raised its flag before the sailing event began.|Câu lạc bộ kéo cờ lên trước khi cuộc thi thuyền buồm bắt đầu.|Countable; raise a flag means move it upwards, often on a pole.|0
licence|official-permission|NOUN|document granting permission|An official permission or document allowing someone to do a particular activity.|giấy phép; sự cho phép chính thức|The stall owner renewed her licence before the summer market opened.|Chủ quầy hàng gia hạn giấy phép trước khi chợ mùa hè mở cửa.|British noun spelling licence; license is the usual American spelling. A licence to do something names the permission.|0
